---
title: "getTempRegistration / QR Access Detection (kintai-v3: Registration Flow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_lookup: GET /register/{token}
    q_lookup --> q_query: SELECT * FROM temp_registrations WHERE qr_token = token
    q_query --> q_not_found: error or no data
    q_not_found --> [*]: return null
    q_query --> q_check_accessed: record found
    q_check_accessed --> q_already_accessed: accessed_at IS NOT NULL
    q_already_accessed --> [*]: return data (no update needed)
    q_check_accessed --> q_first_access: accessed_at IS NULL
    q_first_access --> q_update_accessed: UPDATE temp_registrations SET accessed_at = now() WHERE id = data.id
    q_update_accessed --> [*]: return data (Realtime triggers kiosk screen auto-return)

    note right of q_first_access
        INV-001: First QR scan updates accessed_at, triggering Supabase Realtime event
        INV-002: Kiosk subscribes to temp_registrations via Realtime and auto-returns to idle on accessed_at change
        INV-003: Uses server client for SELECT but admin client for UPDATE (RLS bypass)
        INV-004: temp_registrations table is published to supabase_realtime
    end note
